    doc('CONDITIONAL_RESPONSE_AUDIT.md',f'''# Conditional response audit\n\nFor all pointwise four-group predictions, the historical B component is invariant (maximum group-to-group deviation {bdev:.3e} mV). Thus changes arise through the frozen FiLM-conditioned C component. q changes propagate through the physical mixture reconstruction into I mean/I std/J before the existing FiLM response. This demonstrates an internal frozen-model input-propagation mechanism only, not an electrochemical causal pathway.\n\nEvidence: `outputs/response/condition_response_components.csv`.''')
